purpose: CSS tokenizing, parsing, selectors. Spec-literal, because CSS error recovery is normative.

allow: util dom gfx

public: Token.h Tokenizer.h StyleSheet.h ComputedStyle.h StyleResolver.h MediaQuery.h

extern:

max_tu_lines: 900

# The scanner counts the nested `enum class Kind` as a class of its own. Useful
# rather than a false positive: it is the spec's token list, and a token kind
# added without a parser branch for it is a silent gap.
budget: Kind             header_lines=35 public_methods=0  members=0
# One member for `has_sign`: whether a numeric token was written with an
# explicit sign. The An+B microsyntax of `:nth-child()` is the one CSS grammar
# where `+3` and `3` are not the same token, and the difference cannot be
# recovered from the value once the tokenizer has dropped it.
budget: Token            header_lines=55 public_methods=2  members=6
# Two members for the functional pseudo-classes of ADR 0016 §1: a nested
# selector list for `:is()`/`:where()`/`:not()`, and the An+B of `:nth-child()`.
# The ADR predicted this budget would fire and said why it should: a selector
# list inside a selector list is a new kind of thing to store, and it is what
# turns matching from a loop into a recursion.
budget: SelectorPart     header_lines=50 public_methods=2  members=6
budget: NthPattern       header_lines=20 public_methods=2  members=4
budget: CompoundSelector header_lines=25 public_methods=2  members=2
budget: Specificity      header_lines=30 public_methods=4  members=3
# Raised for DynamicStates, which is the key an invalidation index files a rule
# under. A method on the selector rather than a walk inside the index, so that
# the two cannot disagree about which pseudo-class name means which state --
# a rule filed under a name nothing sets is a rule that never re-applies.
budget: Selector         header_lines=40 public_methods=6  members=1
# Three members for `calc()`: a coefficient, the unit it is a coefficient of,
# and the absolute pixels added to it. `calc(100% - 20px)` is the form the
# feature is overwhelmingly used in and it is two terms, so a one-term Length
# could only have stored it by rounding one of them away. The alternative --
# a full expression tree per length -- would have put an allocation on the type
# four of which sit in every Edges, for a grammar whose measured depth is one.
budget: Length           header_lines=45 public_methods=10 members=3
# One member per property, plus one grouped member for the twelve flex
# properties. Twelve loose fields would have been more than a third of this
# struct and would have said nothing about belonging together; grouped, the
# member count went up by one and the header by the description of what the
# container reads and what the item reads.
# A property bag, and it grows one member per CSS property this engine
# supports -- which is the point of it. The member count is therefore a measure
# of coverage rather than of design, and the numbers that say whether this is
# becoming something other than a property bag are the method count and whether
# any group of fields is large enough to want a struct of its own. Two already
# do: `background` and `flex`.
# Grew by one member and two methods for custom properties, which are a new
# *kind* of stored value rather than one more property: unparsed text, kept as
# text because what `--x: 20px` means depends on where it is substituted. ADR
# 0014 has the measurement that made them the first CSS work to do.
# One method and its reasoning for `display: inline-block`: IsAtomicInline,
# which carries the blockification rule -- a float or an absolutely positioned
# box is not on a line at all, so it is not an atomic inline whatever it was
# declared as. It sits beside IsInlineLevel, which states the same rule for the
# same reason: applied at each call site, one of them eventually forgets.
budget: ComputedStyle    header_lines=225 public_methods=25 members=31
budget: FlexStyle        header_lines=50  public_methods=2  members=12
# The third member is the invalidation index of ADR 0016 §3: which dynamic
# states any rule in this cascade depends on, and which of those can move a box.
# It is on the resolver because it is a property of *the cascade* rather than of
# any one sheet -- the question a change asks is "could anything have changed",
# and one index per sheet would mean asking it once per sheet.
budget: StyleResolver    header_lines=65 public_methods=13 members=3
# The index itself. Two members and they are the two answers ADR 0016 §3
# separates: what any rule depends on, and what a rule that can move a box
# depends on. Collapsing them loses "a hover that changes only colour does not
# run layout", which is the second of the ADR's two properties.
budget: StyleInvalidation header_lines=45 public_methods=6 members=2
